  "interpretation": [
    "The missing finite-step value is front-loaded but not concentrated enough for a three- or six-layer patch. Layers 0-2 recover only 42.4% to roughly half of the gap; layers 0-5 still fall to 69.0% on the worst held-out window.",
    "Every exact single-layer rescue beats fresh88 on all four held-out windows, including layers 10 and 11. The direction deficit is therefore distributed across the entire depth rather than caused by a small set of pathological layers.",
    "The layer ranking is strictly depth ordered on the fit window, with layer 0 largest and layer 11 smallest. This suggests early expansion maps are more sensitive, but it does not justify leaving later layers unchanged.",
    "The current dense c_fc weight's rank-64 left and right singular subspaces capture only 2.69% and 6.77% of residual energy and recover about 3-6% of held-out CE value. Their joint rank-64 core is effectively empty at 0.21% energy and 0-0.3% CE recovery.",
    "The repair is not a current-weight spectral core, per-channel modulation, small residual rank, trust scaling, or a few-layer adapter. A new chart must provide distributed layer-wise directional freedom with bases not restricted to the current weight singular frame."
